t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Last night, President Donald J. Trump delivered a message of American resurgence in an exclusive live interview on Fox News from Shenzhen, China — just hours before his historic meeting with President Xi Jinping and President Vladimir Putin.</strong> He highlighted the respect America now commands under his leadership, the decisive steps he is taking to modernize critical infrastructure, America’s clear lead in Super Intelligence, and his confidence in working with Congress over the next two years as he negotiates from a position of strength.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Key moments:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>On China and President Xi:</strong> “The relationship that I have with China is a great one. You know, it’s a friendship relationship. It’s a respect relationship. You saw the seating last night. You saw the greeting yesterday… This is a great President, one of the great Presidents of China, and he’s never gone to the airport to meet somebody — and not only that, the fanfare, the beauty, the pageantry, the thousands of people… the soldiers, the whole thing. It was a great respect, and I appreciate that. That’s a big win for us. It’s a big win for China, too.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123215548075192560\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On air traffic control:</strong> “This is 50-year-old equipment, and it has to be changed… They spent billions of dollars, the previous Administration, and then they tried to hook it up and it didn’t work; not only didn’t it work, it set it back. So, we want it fixed, and we want it fixed right… When it’s finished, we will have the best system anywhere in the world.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123213109598810455\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On recent tech outages:</strong> “Everything’s good. These are individual events… I also think that the press is sort of having a lot of fun with it. If these things would have happened two years ago, three years ago in the Biden Administration, which was grossly incompetent and corrupt, nobody would have mentioned it… If anybody did that to us and we found out about it, they know what the repercussions would be with me. Nobody’s going to play games with us.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123213992139034978\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On Iran:</strong> “They want to make a deal, but I want a deal that can be lasting… If we have a bad President, a weak President, I want a deal that will supersede the President… One way or the other, we’ll finish it off.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123221203812811092\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On working with Democrats in the new Congress:</strong> “I’ve been called by Democrats at a level that’s pretty amazing. Nobody would even believe it… They want to make deals. I have the veto power… I have a feeling that this is going to be an unbelievably productive two years. Because they’ll send me a bill on healthcare, and I’ll say no way, and I’ll veto it, and then they’ll call me… and we’ll sit down.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123222245325590850\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On Super Intelligence</strong>: “I was with President Xi all night last night, sitting next to him at the dinner, right on his right-hand side, and we spoke the whole evening, and we talked about that, and he’s amazed at how well we’ve done with that. We’re leading China, we’re leading the whole world.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123217406462210127\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On reports of an Iranian dirty bomb plot:</strong> “There is indication that Iran is looking at gas and they’re looking at the bio — the biological weapons, not nice — and other things, and we’ll see&#8230; These are nasty people… Look, if it does happen, we wipe them out.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123219231051288808\">Watch</a>)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>On Obama driving China and Russia together:</strong> “The relationship should have never been allowed to happen. You know, they were natural enemies, but because of Obama, not Biden, it was Obama before, he drove them together because of energy. … All my life I read you never want to have Russia and China team up… What can I tell you? They both like Trump.” (<a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2123220226934178120\">Watch</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/icymi-president-trump-talks-china-iran-super-intelligence-and-the-path-ahead-in-exclusive-interview-from-shenzhen/\">ICYMI: President Trump Talks China, Iran, Super Intelligence, and the Path Ahead in Exclusive Interview from Shenzhen</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
